00:31:22,222 --> 00:31:28,222
Peter Pan is a 1953 American animated adventure fantasy film produced by
Walt Disney Productions and released by RKO Radio Pictures.

12
00:34:13,333 --> 00:34:19,333
Based on J.

13
00:37:04,444 --> 00:37:10,444
Barrie's 1904 play of the same name, the film was directed by
Hamilton Luske, Clyde Geronimi, and Wilfred Jackson.

14
00:39:55,555 --> 00:40:01,555
Featuring the voices of Bobby Driscoll, Kathryn Beaumont, Hans Conried, Bill Thompson, Heather Angel, Paul Collins, Tommy Luske, Candy Candido, Tom Conway, Roland Dupreee and Don Barclay, the film's plot follows
Wendy Darling and her two brothers, who meet the eternally-young Peter Pan and travel with him to the island of Never Land to stay young, where they also have to face Peter's archenemy, Captain Hook.

15
00:42:46,666 --> 00:42:52,666
In 1935, Walt Disney began considering plans to adapt
Barrie's play into an animated feature.

16
00:45:37,777 --> 00:45:43,777
He purchased the film rights from Paramount Pictures in 1938, and
began preliminary development in the next year.

17
00:48:28,888 --> 00:48:34,888
However, following the attack on Pearl Harbor, Disney shelved the project when his studio was
contracted by the United States government to produce training and war propaganda films.

18
00:51:20,000 --> 00:51:26,000
The project sat idle in development for the rest of the
decade until it experienced a turnaround in 1949.

19
00:54:11,111 --> 00:54:17,111
To assist the animators, live-action reference footage
was shot with actors on soundstages.

20
00:57:02,222 --> 00:57:08,222
It also marked the last Disney film in which all nine members of
Disney's Nine Old Men worked together as directing animators.

21
00:59:53,333 --> 00:59:59,333
Peter Pan was released on February 5, 1953, becoming the final Disney animated feature
released through RKO before Disney founded his own distribution company.

22
01:02:44,444 --> 01:02:50,444
The film was entered into the 1953 Cannes Film Festival, Upon its release, the film
earned positive reviews from film critics and was a box office success.

23
01:05:35,555 --> 01:05:41,555
Its representation of the Native Americans received retrospective criticism.

24
01:08:26,666 --> 01:08:32,666
A sequel, titled Return to Never Land, was released in 2002, and a series of
direct-to-DVD prequels focusing on Tinker Bell began in 2008.

25
01:11:17,777 --> 01:11:23,777
A live-action adaptation of the film was released on Disney+ in 2023.

26
01:14:08,888 --> 01:14:14,888
The film explores themes of london, england, sibling
relationship, flying, becoming an adult, magic.
